ocked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/25","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/milestone/25","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/25/labels","id":15520464,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4A7NLQ","number":25,"title":"4.8","description":"","creator":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"open_issues":351,"closed_issues":2337,"state":"open","created_at":"2026-04-13T15:59:35Z","updated_at":"2026-10-22T15:17:38Z","due_on":null,"closed_at":null},"comments":0,"created_at":"2025-10-12T02:10:43Z","updated_at":"2026-10-19T16:57:26Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Tested on Godot 4.4\n- Based on my reading of the Godot source, this issue exists currently in Godot 4.5 and also in previous versions: Godot 4.3 and at least some prior versions.\n\n### System information\n\nWindows 11 - Godot 4.4 - Forward+ renderer - NVIDIA GPU GeForce RTX 3050 Laptop\n\n### Issue description\n\nAccording to [NodePath's Documentation](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/classes/class_nodepath.html#class-nodepath-method-slice), NodePath should have a method called `slice`. Indeed, it does have that method if you are developing with GDScript. However, if a developer wishes to use the C# version of `Slice`, the developer will find that their code will not compile. Apparently, the `Slice` method does not exist in the C# `NodePath` API.\n\nGiven the documentation, the C# version of `NodePath` should have a `Slice` method.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Create a new project in Godot Mono.\n2. Go to **Tools > C# > Create C# Solution**\n3. Create a new C# Script.\n4. Add a method that takes a `NodePath` as a parameter\n5. Attempt to call `Slice` on that parameter.\n6. Attempt to build the project.\n\nThe build will fail.\n\nYou can also create a similar GDScript that also calls `NodePath`'s `slice` method to verify that it is present in the GDScript version.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[TestCSharp.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/22868482/TestCSharp.zip)\n\nThis project includes both a C# and a GDScript variant to demonstrate the differences in the APIs.","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111540/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111540/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null}